// Title: Token anomalies (SYSTEM shells, potato escalation)
// Severity: High
// Why: A cmd/powershell running as SYSTEM inside a user's session (PsExec -s -i, sticky-keys backdoor), a SYSTEM process started by a service account such as IIS AppPool/NETWORK SERVICE (SeImpersonate "potato" exploits), or explorer/sihost running as SYSTEM.
// FalsePositives: Remote management agents that open SYSTEM consoles on purpose. The token user is the first SID reported by getsids.
// MITRE: T1134.001, T1068, T1546.008
// Refs: https://jlajara.gitlab.io/Potatoes_Windows_Privesc ; https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1134/004/
Det_Identity()
